marta: Heads-up — I'm about to merge the TF change that switches our secret sync from creating ExternalSecret objects to directly writing Kubernetes Secrets in target namespaces. Quick Q: does anyone know if our rotation hook (the one that calls the vault agent) depends on the ExternalSecret CRD annotations to trigger incremental rotations?

oliver: We have a small dependency: vault-sync looks for the annotation `external-secrets.redwood.io/last-rotation` to decide whether to run the incremental update path. If that annotation is missing it falls back to a full replace which can bounce pods.

samir: hmm — do we really need to keep the extsecrets annotation? We could copy it into the k8s Secret meta as `redwood.io/last-rotation` during the sync. That would preserve the incremental path without keeping the CR.

leah: +1 for compatibility layer. Also, be careful with our TF change: the module that creates the secrets uses `lifecycle { replace_on_change = true }` in a few places — that will force secret rotation on any metadata change and cause restarts. Can you paste the diff?

marta: pasted — here's the relevant snippet from the module change:
